=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The helpdesk ticket's premise is incorrect. The sshswitch SVIs for VLAN 5
and VLAN 6 are not down — they are fully operational. Direct inspection of
sshswitch shows br_v5 (10.5.0.254/24) and br_v6 (10.6.0.254/24) both in
UP state with their IP addresses correctly assigned and active. The VLAN
802.1q trunking between sshswitch and switch4 is also intact: on the
sshswitch side, eth0.5 and eth0.6 sub-interfaces are UP and bridged into
the respective VLAN bridge domains; on the switch4 side, the matching
eth0.5/eth0.6 sub-interfaces are likewise UP and bridged into br_vlan5 and
br_vlan6. End-to-end data-plane verification confirms 0% packet loss from
VLAN 5 hosts pc1 and pc2 to their default gateway 10.5.0.254, and from
VLAN 6 hosts pc3 and pc4 to their default gateway 10.6.0.254, all with
sub-millisecond to low-millisecond round-trip times. There is no injected
fault, no misconfiguration, and no interface state anomaly present anywhere
in the reported path. The root cause of the ticket is a false premise: the
reporter's belief that the SVIs dropped after a reload does not reflect the
actual live state of the lab. No corrective action is needed; the network
is healthy and the gateways are reachable by all VLAN 5 and VLAN 6 clients.
=== END ===
```